        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "358fb678-cb3e-35a3-91b4-5f23407f15c1",
                "word": "mutuellement",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9225b021-e20b-37c3-b472-5340a8f51881",
                        "entry_id": "358fb678-cb3e-35a3-91b4-5f23407f15c1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "D’une manière mutuelle ; réciproquement."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3e9003ba-427c-40c4-a2e8-b88aad88041a",
                                "sense_id": "9225b021-e20b-37c3-b472-5340a8f51881",
                                "text": "Il pourrait arriver que plusieurs personnes, sans former actuellement une société en nom collectif, convinssent d'en former une à une certaine époque, jetassent les bases de cette société future, et se promissent mutuellement, sous peine de payer une certaine somme à titre de dédit, de régulariser la constitution de cette société par la rédaction d'un acte écrit et par l'accomplissement des formalités de publication."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0a34d66d-e890-40a4-86c9-b76083c11fbe",
                                "sense_id": "9225b021-e20b-37c3-b472-5340a8f51881",
                                "text": "Puis sans considérer aucune différence entre ces lignes connues et inconnues, on doit parcourir la difficulté selon l’ordre qui montre, le plus naturellement de tous, en quelle sorte elles [des lignes, dans un problème de géométrie] dépendent mutuellement les unes des autres."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6ad9acf-76b7-4f5a-aedb-d65c7cc11a58",
                                "sense_id": "9225b021-e20b-37c3-b472-5340a8f51881",
                                "text": "L’accumulation des critères et l’émiettement des dotations et sous-dotations ne permettent plus de percevoir la direction principale de la péréquation, quand les choix devenus trop nombreux ne se neutralisent pas mutuellement."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6043bd6-ba75-458e-9918-a8f49af40581",
                                "sense_id": "9225b021-e20b-37c3-b472-5340a8f51881",
                                "text": "C’est ainsi qu’ils se donnaient mutuellement un repos qui les appliquait chacun tout entier à son action."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6a335cb4-d9b3-4668-9f7b-566df4aa07eb",
                                "sense_id": "9225b021-e20b-37c3-b472-5340a8f51881",
                                "text": "Les poëtes, et ceux qu’on nomme littérateurs, sont presque les seuls artistes auxquels on puisse reprocher ce ridicule de se déchirer mutuellement sans raison."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d3621f4d-fa6b-3a33-9693-c5910e45bd1e",
                        "entry_id": "358fb678-cb3e-35a3-91b4-5f23407f15c1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "L'un par rapport à l'autre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "37710d60-b492-4231-9b82-f257601d0a34",
                                "sense_id": "d3621f4d-fa6b-3a33-9693-c5910e45bd1e",
                                "text": "Aujourd'hui, nous savons que les deux rayons réfractés par un cristal biréfringent sont polarisés linéairement dans des directions mutuellement perpendiculaires; […]."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "91475f6d-ab7b-42ea-99bf-a5c029b705a4",
                        "source_entry_id": "358fb678-cb3e-35a3-91b4-5f23407f15c1",
                        "target_lang_word": "gegenseitig",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gegenseitig",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1bd5d2b4-b1ab-3da5-8085-a82a4a81150b",
                                        "entry_id": "2f6c50f5-2547-398d-a044-df457d52764f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "so, dass zwischen zwei Menschen oder Dingen ein für beide Seiten gleichermaßen geltendes Geschehen erfolgt"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2cd38464-ad8f-4f36-9bdb-59f23c1ff56c",
                                                "sense_id": "1bd5d2b4-b1ab-3da5-8085-a82a4a81150b",
                                                "text": "Wir müssen uns gegenseitig helfen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a1fee13-dffd-4ef9-8bb8-2061a12f20e5",
                                                "sense_id": "1bd5d2b4-b1ab-3da5-8085-a82a4a81150b",
                                                "text": "Zu einer guten menschlichen Beziehung gehört eine gegenseitige Rücksichtnahme."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e3ea389-4970-4e28-bc44-06f4e3082df5",
                                                "sense_id": "1bd5d2b4-b1ab-3da5-8085-a82a4a81150b",
                                                "text": "„Der Noniusgrenzwinkel ist der kleinste Sehwinkel, unter dem eine gegenseitige Versetzung von Objekten in einer frontoparallelen Ebene erkennbar wird.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1809cef4-e6e3-4bdd-8270-d43acc794d89",
                        "source_entry_id": "358fb678-cb3e-35a3-91b4-5f23407f15c1",
                        "target_lang_word": "einer dem anderen",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d7d82ba9-5158-4a87-92f0-1e0d1807ffc8",
                        "source_entry_id": "358fb678-cb3e-35a3-91b4-5f23407f15c1",
                        "target_lang_word": "each other",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "each other",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2da3c710-7174-3b9c-9abb-00993b43ad51",
                                        "entry_id": "fbff04ee-7061-379c-a3d6-78408300d13a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To one another; one to the other; signifies that a verb applies to two or more entities both as subjects and as direct objects"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "pronoun",
                                            "reciprocal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e44ea647-a005-4ca6-8777-fe6faaa76631",
                                                "sense_id": "2da3c710-7174-3b9c-9abb-00993b43ad51",
                                                "text": "My parents love each other; however, they talk to themselves a lot but not so much to each other."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f390dbdc-43c2-48ad-ab7a-9744f38081d9",
                                                "sense_id": "2da3c710-7174-3b9c-9abb-00993b43ad51",
                                                "text": "I don't think you two know each other, do you?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f783839-0cec-4e31-b074-1af1cfa9dd4c",
                                                "sense_id": "2da3c710-7174-3b9c-9abb-00993b43ad51",
                                                "text": "Now we plunged into a deep shade with the boughs lacing each other overhead, and crossed dainty, rustic bridges over the cold trout-streams, the boards giving back the clatter of our horses' feet: or anon we shot into a clearing, with a colored glimpse of the lake and its curving shore far below us."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43362fb9-8f41-45db-846e-d917f2354901",
                                                "sense_id": "2da3c710-7174-3b9c-9abb-00993b43ad51",
                                                "text": "There is an hour or two, after the passengers have embarked, which is disquieting and fussy.[…]Passengers wander restlessly about or hurry, with futile energy, from place to place. Pushing men hustle each other at the windows of the purser's office, under pretence of expecting letters or despatching telegrams."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5983f92-939f-4572-beea-4ab7193d00f0",
                                                "sense_id": "2da3c710-7174-3b9c-9abb-00993b43ad51",
                                                "text": "We've known each other many years, but this is the first time you ever came to me for counsel or for help."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49bf8472-471e-4447-a346-6366a63411f5",
                                                "sense_id": "2da3c710-7174-3b9c-9abb-00993b43ad51",
                                                "text": "It was the first time United had conceded six goals at Old Trafford since 1930, when Huddersfield won 6-0 and Newcastle 7-4 within four days of each other."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "60a29ce4-6a4a-4b44-8bf3-f34f042760c2",
                        "source_entry_id": "358fb678-cb3e-35a3-91b4-5f23407f15c1",
                        "target_lang_word": "mutually",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mutually",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a4b4fb9-b9a6-354b-9c0e-e52a14d5a088",
                                        "entry_id": "2783b676-0f7f-3605-9c19-542be1c1f79e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In the same way, each to the other; reciprocally"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ead45f6f-5504-4feb-bc18-8e81a2c6eba3",
                                                "sense_id": "2a4b4fb9-b9a6-354b-9c0e-e52a14d5a088",
                                                "text": "The contract was mutually binding."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0da2a8c-3bf9-4ad4-91a1-dde850d1cb46",
                                                "sense_id": "2a4b4fb9-b9a6-354b-9c0e-e52a14d5a088",
                                                "text": "Each written word when spoken is mutually incomprehensible between a Mandarin speaker in Beijing and a Cantonese speaker in Hong Kong. If you think that’s odd, consider our number system: the symbol “9” is universally recognized but it’s pronounced “nine” in English and “devet” in Slovenian."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7bb357df-947c-4bb1-86c3-1cd4c155bd41",
                                                "sense_id": "2a4b4fb9-b9a6-354b-9c0e-e52a14d5a088",
                                                "text": "The deepening strategic partnership between the People’s Republic of China and the Russian Federation and their mutually reinforcing attempts to undercut the rules-based international order run counter to our values and interests."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4dde9515-f789-3419-b474-71381dd9a148",
                                        "entry_id": "2783b676-0f7f-3605-9c19-542be1c1f79e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a shared manner; equally; affecting all parties the same way"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49741117-a1d6-4c99-aebd-a9f810e61c18",
                                                "sense_id": "4dde9515-f789-3419-b474-71381dd9a148",
                                                "text": "The adventure was mutually beneficial."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8984aec9-96e2-4215-8389-dc110d081931",
                        "source_entry_id": "358fb678-cb3e-35a3-91b4-5f23407f15c1",
                        "target_lang_word": "one another",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "one another",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7770eac7-5a12-3d57-839f-9c4454936146",
                                        "entry_id": "7e1257d8-bd3a-3f9e-bcff-7467b2e2289c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used of a reciprocal relationship among a group of two or more people or things; compare each other."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "pronoun",
                                            "reciprocal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72008528-c193-42ec-bbeb-d8f0f4efa39a",
                                                "sense_id": "7770eac7-5a12-3d57-839f-9c4454936146",
                                                "text": "The raw recruits helped one another get over the first few days."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70841139-deb5-42e1-8b9b-d0299501d5aa",
                                                "sense_id": "7770eac7-5a12-3d57-839f-9c4454936146",
                                                "text": "Rainy days seemed to follow one another all summer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d90c4b89-9e47-40d7-a396-987f498d46aa",
                                                "sense_id": "7770eac7-5a12-3d57-839f-9c4454936146",
                                                "text": "It is here within the state borders of Ukraine that we can confirm the strength of the borders of all European countries. We can guarantee that nobody will dare to return tyranny to our continent. It is here that the values of our Eur-Atlantic community have been revived by a people that is fighting for freedom and with other nations that help us in the struggle. We are real allies with NATO. We have covered this road to NATO. And in actual fact, we have proven that we are compatible with the standards of the alliance. They are real on the battlefield in every aspect of our cooperation. We trust one another, we help one another, and we are protecting, defending one another and that is our alliance. This is an actual alliance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
